WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:03.270
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here.

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:07.899
Although we've seen all the trailers for Infinity
War, Marvel still haven't revealed who Game

00:00:07.899 --> 00:00:10.299
of Thrones star Peter Dinklage will be playing
in the film.

00:00:10.299 --> 00:00:14.480
So, today, I'm going to give you a breakdown
of who his mystery character is most likely

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.480
to be.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.029
And I'm kicking off a brand new Avengers giveaway.

00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:22.680
To enter you just need to be a subscriber
and leave me a comment here about the movie.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:27.070
Also remember to ring the bell to make sure
you get all my new videos!

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.710
MCU speculation and mild spoilers ahead for
Thor in Infinity War.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:36.250
The character Peter Dinklage could well be
playing in the movie is Eitri, King of the

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.680
Dwarves of Nidavellir, which is one of the
Nine Realms.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:44.020
Eitri, who's a master blacksmith, was first
introduced in the Thor comics in the early

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:49.890
1980s and later appeared on the animated TV
series, The Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:54.570
In the Infinity War movie, Thor travels to
Nidavellir in search of a new weapon.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:59.050
And in the comics, there is a bond between
Nidavellir and Asgard; indeed, it's the dwarves

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:04.199
who create Thor's hammer Mjolnir as well as
an axe-like hammer called Stormbreaker, which

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:06.530
will be Thor's new weapon in the movie.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:10.810
In terms of the MCU, the dwarves of Nidavellir
have already made a brief appearance in the

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:15.680
prelude comic to Thor: The Dark World, where
they feared an attack by trolls on their forges

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.310
because Asgard couldn't protect them after
the destruction of the Bifrost.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:24.550
But the dwarves may well play a bigger part
in the Infinity War movie, as there are rumours

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:28.780
that they also created the Infinity Gauntlet
and that there have been casting calls for

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.010
actors of short stature.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:35.549
Another possibility is that Dinklage will
play Pip the Troll, a prince who was transformed

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:38.660
into a troll and who loved to drink and have
a good time.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:43.439
The character was created by artist-writer
Jim Starlin who also gave us Thanos, Drax

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:45.380
the Destroyer, and Gamora.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:49.979
Pip's appearances in the comics include the
Infinity Gauntlet storyline and he's a member

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:54.799
of the Infinity Watch which was put together
by Adam Warlock to protect the Infinity Gems.

00:01:54.799 --> 00:02:00.259
On top of that, he's also had his mind destroyed
by Thanos, but Adam Warlock came to the rescue,

00:02:00.259 --> 00:02:04.860
absorbing Pip's soul into the Soul Gem where
he lived in Soulworld until he was restored

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.369
into the real world via the body of a recently
deceased human.

00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:13.170
Now, Adam Warlock's introduction to the MCU
was teased in a Guardians of the Galaxy 2

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:18.410
post-credits scene, however, according to
James Gunn, Warlock won't appear till Guardians

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:19.410
3.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:23.740
But that doesn't necessarily rule Pip out
of Infinity War because, in addition to Pip's

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:28.530
comic-book connections with Thanos, Gamora,
and the Infinity Gems, early last year Peter

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:32.910
Dinklage was spotted getting his hair dyed
red, which is just the right colour to play

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.460
Pip the Troll!

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:39.030
There's also a chance that Dinklage is lending
his voice to one of Thanos's Black Order.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:43.310
In an interview with Vulture, Kevin Feige
said 'there are interesting people doing the

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.310
voices.'

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.980
So far, it looks like Terry Notary and Tom
Vaughan-Lawlor will be playing two of the

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.370
Black Order, possibly Cull Obsidian and Ebony
Maw.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:55.560
Maybe Dinklage will voice Corvus Glaive, who
we already saw in the trailers attacking Vision

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.620
for the Mind Stone with his blade.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:01.850
Dinklage would certainly fall into the category
of 'interesting people' that Feige mentions,

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:05.850
however, you'd think they might prefer to
give such a well-known actor a visual rather

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:10.860
than a vocal role; then again we do have Bradley
Cooper as the voice of Rocket and James Spader

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:11.860
was Ultron.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:16.090
So, maybe they think a voice role would potentially
cause less confusion for people who remember

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:20.150
Dinklage as Bolivar Trask in X-Men: Days of
Future Past.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:24.810
After all, Josh Brolin, for example, plays
Thanos in the MCU through motion-capture and

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:30.300
voice work, but in Deadpool 2 he plays another
Marvel Comics character, Cable, on screen.

